[Unit]
Description=Daily Trivy CVE scan of container images
Documentation=file:///home/pi/Projects/Server/4-Security-Monitoring/README.md

[Timer]
# Daily 04:10, no random delay: the image lists of beefy and tower are read over ssh in the first seconds, while beefy is up (03:55 to 04:45); the Trivy part then runs on fastpi against the registry and needs neither host. Daily (was weekly 2026-10-21): a fresh CVE like PHP2Shell must not wait up to 6 days for the next scan; the DB refresh + ~60 image scans cost a few minutes at 04:10 when the Pi is idle, and NewCriticalImageVulnerabilities (security-posture.yml) then pages within a day of a new fixable critical appearing.
OnCalendar=*-*-* 04:10:00
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
